{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791432959,"nonce":"jkCZdcNtziaU3c9P7nyvyYrK1ec=","title":"Field reads through String and Array type constraints use object reflection","message":"Issue10343 defines foo\u003cT:String\u003e(str:T):Int returning str.length. The 897 baseline returns 0 for hello instead of 5. With stable root-package reflection identities, the same unsupported native String/object reflection mismatch produces a native crash in both Application and pinned Cranelift modes.\n\nThe MIR shows foo__String retains an i64 argument and calls haxe_reflect_field on its raw String pointer. MIR specialization does not rewrite that reflection call into native String field access. String and Array type constraints identify the native reference layout, so their fields should use the same lowering as concrete references. Structural constraints must keep their existing reflection path.\n\nConstrainedReferenceFields.hx covers nonempty and empty constrained String and Array values plus a String typedef constraint. It passes native Haxe. Prototype v9 uses nominal reference constraints for field lowering; release and corpus validation are pending.\n\nArtifacts: /tmp/rayzor-macro-probe-final-v8/logs/Issue10343.log, /tmp/rayzor-enum-reflection-final-v8/logs/Issue10343.log, /tmp/rayzor-issue10343-repeat-v8.log, /tmp/rayzor-issue10343-pinned-v8.log, /tmp/rayzor-issue10343-mir-v8.log, /tmp/rayzor-constrained-reference-native-v9.log.","files":null}]}